---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL, PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_URL, PRIVACY_EMAIL } from '../../data/pantrybaby';
import { COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME, COMPANY_DBA } from '../../data/legal';

// Every statement on this page must stay true of the PantryBaby v1 source.
// Audit trail: Integrator .ai-council/dap/runs/2026-10-20 CRM launch validation (D-02..D-05).
const lastUpdated = 'October 20, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="PantryBaby Privacy Policy"
  description="PantryBaby privacy policy: what the app collects, when, who processes it, how deletion works across your BabyBlocks account, and your rights."
  canonical="/pantrybaby/privacy"
  theme="pantry"
  product="pantrybaby"
>
  <div class="policy-layout">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <div class="policy-header">
        <a href="/pantrybaby" class="policy-back">← PantryBaby</a>
        <div class="label-chip" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">Legal</div>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="policy-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated} · Applies to PantryBaby for iOS</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-summary glass">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You can use PantryBaby without an account. In that mode your pantry stays on your device.</li>
          <li>If you sign in, PantryBaby uses your BabyBlocks account, the same account BudgetBaby uses. Cloud Sync is on by default for signed-in users and you can turn it off.</li>
          <li>Usage data is off unless you turn it on. It never includes item, list or store names. PantryBaby does not collect crash reports and does not track you across apps.</li>
          <li>We don't sell data, show ads, or share your shopping history.</li>
          <li>Delete your PantryBaby data, or your whole BabyBlocks account, in Settings, then About PantryBaby.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-content">

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>1. Your BabyBlocks account</h2>
          <p>
            PantryBaby and BudgetBaby are both BabyBlocks apps and share one sign-in. If you sign in to PantryBaby with
            Apple or Google, you are using your BabyBlocks account. If you already use BudgetBaby with the same Apple or
            Google sign-in, it is the same account. Each app keeps its own data. Signing in to PantryBaby does not give it
            your BudgetBaby data.
          </p>
          <p>
            Signing in is optional. If you choose "Continue without an account", PantryBaby works on this device only.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>2. What we collect, and when</h2>

          <h3>If you don't sign in</h3>
          <p>
            Your pantry, lists and stores stay on your device. We receive nothing unless you contact support (see below).
          </p>

          <h3>If you sign in</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address and, if your sign-in provider shares it, your name. With Sign in with Apple you can choose to share a private relay address instead of your real email.</li>
            <li><strong>Synced data.</strong> With Cloud Sync on, your pantry items, lists, stores and settings are stored in your account so they appear on your other devices. Cloud Sync is on by default when you sign in. You can turn it off in Settings, then Account, then Cloud Sync.</li>
            <li><strong>Subscription status.</strong> If you subscribe to Premium, RevenueCat tells the app whether your subscription is active. RevenueCat identifies you by your BabyBlocks account ID.</li>
            <li><strong>App integrity check.</strong> The app uses Apple's App Attest, through Firebase App Check, to confirm requests come from the genuine app.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Usage data (off unless you turn it on)</h3>
          <p>
            In Settings, then Privacy, "Share usage data" is off by default. If you turn it on, PantryBaby sends which
            screens and features you use (for example "opened Settings" or "added an item") to our own servers to help us
            improve the app. If you are signed in, this is linked to your BabyBlocks account and its email address, and your
            account is recorded as a PantryBaby user. It never sends item, list or store names or anything you type. Turn it
            off at any time and sending stops.
          </p>

          <h3>Support requests</h3>
          <p>
            When you send a request from Settings, then Support, we receive the subject and description you write, your
            account email if you are signed in (or an anonymous identifier made from your device if you are not), and the
            app and iOS version. If you choose to attach a diagnostics report, it contains technical logs about the app.
            Names of your items, lists and stores are removed from those logs before they leave your device. Photos or
            screenshots you attach are sent as you chose them. You can also email us at
            <a href={`mailto:${PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> or use the
            <a href={PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_URL}>support portal</a>.
          </p>

          <h3>Camera and photos</h3>
          <p>
            PantryBaby asks for camera or photo library access only when you choose to add a photo. Photos stay on your
            device. They are not uploaded by Cloud Sync. They are included in a backup only if you create one.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>3. What we do not collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Your location. PantryBaby does not request location access.</li>
            <li>Crash reports. PantryBaby does not include a crash-reporting service.</li>
            <li>Advertising identifiers. PantryBaby does not track you across other companies' apps or websites, and does not show ads.</li>
            <li>Your contacts, calendar or health data.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>4. How your data is stored</h2>

          <h3>On your device</h3>
          <p>
            PantryBaby stores your data on your device, protected by iOS data protection.
          </p>

          <h3>Cloud Sync</h3>
          <p>
            Synced data is stored in Google Cloud Firestore under your account, sent over encrypted connections and
            encrypted at rest by Google. It is not end-to-end encrypted, which means it is technically readable by our
            systems. We access it only to operate the service, to help you when you ask us to, or when the law requires it.
          </p>

          <h3>Backups</h3>
          <p>
            Backups are optional and are encrypted on your device with AES-256-GCM before they are saved or uploaded.
            The encryption key is kept in your iOS Keychain, which can sync it through iCloud Keychain so you can restore on
            a new device. Cloud backups are stored in Firebase Storage under your account. We cannot read an encrypted
            backup without your key.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>5. Who processes your data</h2>
          <div class="policy-table-wrap">
            <table class="policy-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Service</th>
                  <th>Purpose</th>
                  <th>Data involved</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Google Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage, App Check)</td>
                  <td>Sign-in, Cloud Sync, backups, app integrity</td>
                  <td>Account email and ID, synced data, encrypted backups</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Sign in with Apple, Google Sign-In</td>
                  <td>Signing in</td>
                  <td>What you allow Apple or Google to share, usually email and an account ID</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>RevenueCat and Apple</td>
                  <td>Subscriptions and purchases</td>
                  <td>Account ID, purchase and subscription status. Apple handles payment</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Cloudflare (our servers at babyblocks.io)</td>
                  <td>Support requests, usage data if you turned it on, service status</td>
                  <td>Support messages and diagnostics, usage events</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Microsoft 365</td>
                  <td>Support email</td>
                  <td>Emails you send us and our replies</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>We do not sell your data and we do not use it for advertising.</p>
          <p>
            Google processes data for us under the <a href="https://firebase.google.com/terms/data-processing-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Data Processing and Security Terms</a>,
            and RevenueCat under its <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/dpa" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data Processing Agreement</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>6. Email from us</h2>
          <p>
            We email you about your support requests and, if you subscribe, about your subscription. We send PantryBaby news
            only if you asked for it, for example by joining the PantryBaby waitlist. Using BudgetBaby does not sign you up
            for PantryBaby email. Every marketing email has an unsubscribe link.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section" id="deletion">
          <h2>7. Deleting your data</h2>
          <p>Go to Settings, then About PantryBaby, then Delete Data or Account. You can choose:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Delete PantryBaby data.</strong> Removes your PantryBaby cloud data and backups, and the PantryBaby data on this device. Your BabyBlocks account and your BudgetBaby data are kept.</li>
            <li><strong>Delete BabyBlocks account.</strong> Removes your account, which also ends your access to BudgetBaby and deletes its cloud data, along with all PantryBaby data.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Deleting data or the app does not cancel a subscription. Cancel Premium in your Apple ID settings, under
            Subscriptions.
          </p>
          <p>
            In-app deletion does not remove support requests, usage data or subscription records held on our servers or by
            RevenueCat. To have those deleted, email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
            See also <a href="/pantrybaby/delete-data">how to delete your data</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>8. Your rights and choices</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Access and export.</strong> You can export your PantryBaby data from Settings, then Data &amp; Backup, then Backup &amp; Restore.</li>
            <li><strong>Deletion.</strong> In the app, as described above, or by email.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage data.</strong> Off unless you turn it on, and you can turn it off at any time.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Sync.</strong> You can turn it off at any time.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>For users in the European Economic Area and the UK</h3>
          <p>
            You have the right to access, correct, erase, restrict and port your personal data, to object to processing, to
            withdraw consent at any time, and to complain to your local data protection authority. Our legal bases are
            contract (your account, Cloud Sync, backups and subscription), consent (usage data and marketing email), and
            legitimate interest (answering support requests and keeping the service secure).
          </p>

          <h3 id="ccpa-do-not-sell">For users in California</h3>
          <p>
            You have the right to know what personal information we collect, to correct it, to delete it, and to opt out of
            its sale or sharing. <strong>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information:</strong> we do not sell or share
            personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising, and have not done so in the preceding twelve
            months.
          </p>

          <h3>How to make a request</h3>
          <p>
            Email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a> from the address on your account if you have one,
            and tell us what you would like. You don't need an account to make a request. We respond within 30 days.
          </p>

          <h3>Cookies</h3>
          <p>The PantryBaby app does not use cookies. This website does not set tracking or advertising cookies.</p>

          <h3>How long we keep data</h3>
          <p>
            Data on your device stays until you delete it. Synced data and backups stay while your account exists and are
            deleted when you delete them in the app. Support requests are kept so we can help you with follow-ups, and are
            deleted on request. Usage data is kept until you ask us to delete it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>PantryBaby is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has given us personal information, email <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>If we make material changes, we will update the date at the top of this page and tell you in the app before they take effect.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>11. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Privacy requests and questions: <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.
            App support: <a href={`mailto:${PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Data controller:</strong><br />
            {COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME}, operating as {COMPANY_DBA}
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-layout {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-12));
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }

  .policy-back {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .policy-back:hover { color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
  }

  .policy-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl));
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy-meta {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-summary {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .policy-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-10);
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-section h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .policy-section ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .policy-steps {
    list-style: decimal;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-steps li { padding-left: var(--space-2); }

  .policy-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
  }

  .policy-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
  }

  .policy-table th {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .policy-table td {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .policy-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
</style>
